Catalog changes cost O(account entries) in the browser, not O(entries changed).
Each snapshot or change reloads every resource record of the account from
IndexedDB (`toArray()` in apps/app `indexeddb-resource-metadata.ts`), clones
canonical/parent/classification per record for `catalogObservationFence`
(`catalog-acquisition.ts`), and re-projects the folder tree (`projectRows`).

Measured on the import-workflow branch with a dev account holding 8.8k catalog
entries: a cold note open paints its body after 3-5 s with no import running, and
a note opened across a 3.2k-entry import reveal took 30 s. A profile of a cold
open shows Dexie reads (1.3 s) and `projectRows` (0.8 s) on the main thread.

Fix by diffing against the installed view and writing only changed records, and
keep the fence keyed by revision instead of cloned values. Evidence: work item
`import-workflow`, `evidence/uf-d2-fix2/README.md` (B2, B4).
